.policy "ruff-n804-invalid-first-argument-name-for-class-method" revision 2
.description "Name the first parameter of class methods cls, as PEP 8 recommends, so it reads as the class and not as an instance."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N804 (pep8-naming): a class method whose first positional parameter is not named `cls`. Class methods
// are those decorated @classmethod or @abc.abstractclassmethod (or a `pep8-naming.classmethod-decorators`
// entry), `__init_subclass__` and `__class_getitem__`, and every plain method of a metaclass (a class deriving
// from type, abc.ABCMeta or enum.EnumMeta). Names matching `pep8-naming.ignore-names` are exempt.
//   class C:
//       @classmethod
//       def make(self): ...          ← N804 at `self`
//   class Meta(type):
//       def m(cls): ...              not reported
#include "python/naming.rr"

.violation N804(at: node, x: symbol) code "N804"
    "Rename this class method's first parameter `{x}` to `cls` and update its uses in the body, unless another parameter already has that name; keep it if the project follows another convention."
    suppress ruff "N804"
N804(nm, x) :- naming_method_kind(f, "classmethod"), naming_first_param(f, nm, x), x != "cls", !naming_ignored(x).
